# Ship a Holdfast mod version

A change a player or admin can see is not done until a new patch is released. Do this in the same turn. Do not wait to be asked. Do not stop after editing source.

The downloadable version is the GitHub release, not the files on disk. This repo ignores source. `mod-registry.json` is only the note.

## Set one new patch

Bump the patch on the live release (`1.0.73` becomes `1.0.74`). Write that same number in all of these:

- `ModVersions.json` for that mod
- the mod `.csproj`: `Version`, `AssemblyVersion`, `FileVersion` (`FileVersion` ends in `.0`)
- `[BepInPlugin(..., "x.y.z")]` and the startup log line
- `mod-registry.json` `changelog`, starting with `vX.Y.Z - `

Do not run `build-mod.ps1` or `publish-mod.ps1` to bump. Those scripts increment `ModVersions.json` again, so a version you already set becomes one higher.

## Release it

Build Release with `dotnet build`. Confirm the DLL assembly version. Public mods go to `Xarkanoth/HoldfastMods`. Private mods go to `Xarkanoth/HoldfastPrivateMods`.

MapCapture and CharacterCapture are private. Tag `MapCapture-vX.Y.Z` or `CharacterCapture-vX.Y.Z`, asset the matching DLL, repo `Xarkanoth/HoldfastPrivateMods`.

Copying the DLL into the game plugins folder is not the release. The turn is not done until `gh release create` has succeeded and `mod-registry.json` is pushed.

CharacterCapture's registry note lives in `mod-registry.json` on `Xarkanoth/HoldfastPrivateMods`. Commit and push that file on that repo. Public mods, and MapCapture, stay in this repo's `mod-registry.json`.

```powershell
gh release create AdvancedAdminUI-v1.0.74 AdvancedAdminUI.dll `
  --repo Xarkanoth/HoldfastMods `
  --title "Advanced Admin UI v1.0.74" `
  --notes "One plain sentence about what the player sees."
```

The DLL path is the mod folder's `OutputPath` (usually the Mods root). Notes are the changelog sentence without the `vX.Y.Z - ` prefix.

Commit and push `mod-registry.json` on this repo. Leave source untracked.

Skip the release only when the user says not to publish.
